  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better Protecting Children Affected by Armed Conflict</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 24-month project will enhance UN OSRSG CAAC&#x2019;s engagement with parties to conflict across the 25 situations and one regional monitoring arrangement, leading to increased joint action plans, handover protocols, and other commitments to end grave violations against children. It will strengthen the capacities of governments, conflict parties, and child protection actors through targeted training and capacity-building activities. Additionally, the project will advance worldwide advocacy, including a new global campaign encouraging Member States to publicly pledge commitments to the Convention on the Rights of the Child (CRC), with pledges published by UN OSRSG CAAC.</narrative>
  </description>
